{
  "verdict": "CONCERNS",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Translation cache keeps stale fallback results after `default_locale` changes",
      "description": "`translate` caches no-argument results in an LRU keyed only by `\"#{key}#{config.locale}#{config.backend.object_id}\"` (lines 72\u201376). The fallback chain is not in the key. Before this diff, the chain did not read the site setting. This diff makes it depend on the setting: `FallbackLocaleList#[]` returns `[locale, SiteSetting.default_locale.to_sym, :en]` (config/initializers/i18n.rb:17), and the backend consults that chain on each lookup.\n\nNothing invalidates the cache when `default_locale` changes. The setting is `refresh: true` (config/site_settings.yml:59-62). The admin change path calls `Discourse.request_refresh!` (lib/site_setting_extension.rb:336, lib/discourse.rb:242-248), which only publishes a client-side refresh. `refresh!` calls `clear_cache!` (lib/site_setting_extension.rb:344-347), which clears SiteText and client-settings caches, not the I18n cache. The only path that resets `@cache` is `I18n.reload!` (translate_accelerator.rb:39-41), and no code outside the freedom patch calls it.\n\nPath to a wrong result: user locale `fr`, and key K exists in `en` and `de` but not `fr`. While the default is `en`, the first lookup caches the English string. An admin switches the default to `de`. A fresh lookup now resolves `fr \u2192 de \u2192 en` and returns the German string. This process keeps returning English for K until the entry is evicted (cache size 300) or the process restarts. Other processes hold their own cache and can disagree.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "lib/freedom_patches/translate_accelerator.rb:67-77"
    },
    {
      "severity": "NOTE",
      "title": "Fallbacks now apply in development and test, not only production",
      "description": "The initializer loads on every environment. Before this diff, only `production.rb` and `profile.rb` set `config.i18n.fallbacks = true` (removed in this diff); development and test did not. Now a key missing in the user's locale silently renders the default-locale or English string in development and test. Previously it rendered a visible \"translation missing\" marker. This is probably intended, but it hides missing translations in dev and test, and any specs or manual checks that expect the marker will see different output.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "error-handling-observability",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "config/initializers/i18n.rb:9"
    }
  ],
